    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0376" n="1210" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1210"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/211</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-15T16:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 16, 12.31
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8678. War Trade Board from Sheldon:</p>
                <p>No. 165. Swedish delegates have received word from Swedish Government saying it
                    considers itself not bound by <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> owing
                    to your new bunkering rules<anchor n="1" xml:id="d314-f1"/> of which neither the
                    Swedish delegates here, nor any Allied representatives, had any intimation. The
                        <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> contained the only bunkering
                    arrangements and control of boats that the Swedes are willing to accept, and the
                    Allied position was considered adequately safeguarded by the terms of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>. It is most urgent to have matter
                    settled on account of desire of Swedes to get commodities released, especially
                    phosphate rock in time to be of use for crops, and desire of Allies to use <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> ships. Are you not willing make a
                    declaration that your bunkering rules do not apply to <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >modus vivendi?</hi> Understand British and French are cabling their
                    Washington Embassy. The matter is urgent so please give this immediate
                    attention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
